<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!--
    Choices built as trade-offs from the start: every answer has its own upside and its own cost (work done or not,
    sleep, medicine, food, someone's mood), and the safe answer gives the least. Each comes only when it fits the colony
    as it is: just after a fight, with someone ill and medicine in the stores, at a busy time with a willing student,
    a neighbour short of food in spring. What each answer does is shown under it in the letter.
  -->

  <!-- ===================== The morning after the fight ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_DlmC_AfterTheRaid</defName>
    <label>the mess after the fight</label>
    <weight>1.2</weight>
    <cooldownDays>30</cooldownDays>
    <withinDaysOfThreat>1.5</withinDaysOfThreat>
    <answerDays>1</answerDays>
    <texts>
      <li>The fighting is over, and the colony looks it: blood on the floors, doors off their hinges, things dropped all over the yard. {A_nameDef} wants everyone on it now, before dark. Half the colony can barely stand.</li>
      <li>[night] Nobody has slept. The raiders are gone, but their mess isn't, and {A_nameDef} is already going from door to door with a broom, asking who's coming. Most of the doors stay shut.</li>
      <li>[winter] The cold gets in wherever the raiders broke through, and the yard is strewn with what they left behind. {A_nameDef} says it all has to be cleared today. The others say they need one night first.</li>
    </texts>
    <defaultOption>2</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>Everyone clears up, now</label>
        <outcome>Everyone turned out with brooms and hammers, and the worst of it was cleared by dark. {A_nameDef} thanked each of them by name. Nobody had much to say at supper.</outcome>
        <ways><toil>4</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_WorkParty"><label>the clearing up after the fight</label><target>Colony</target><count>6</count><tasks><li>Corpses</li><li>Clean</li><li>Repair</li><li>Haul</li></tasks><duration>2.5~3.5</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Vindicated</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmR_PutToWork</thought><degreeTrait>Industriousness</degreeTrait><maxDegree>-1</maxDegree></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairsFair</thought><degreeTrait>Industriousness</degreeTrait><minDegree>1</minDegree></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Strain"><target>Colony</target><amount>6</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Rest first; it can wait until tomorrow</label>
        <outcome>The council sent everyone to rest. The mess waits for tomorrow, and {A_nameDef} has spent the afternoon looking at it.</outcome>
        <ways><toil>-4</toil><mercy>2</mercy></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Rest"><target>Colony</target></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Colony</target><thought>Council_DlmR_RestDay</thought><chance>0.4</chance></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmR_IdleDay</thought><degreeTrait>Industriousness</degreeTrait><minDegree>1</minDegree></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Overruled</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_StrainRelief"><target>Colony</target><amount>8</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Three clear what can't wait; the rest rest</label>
        <outcome>Three of them cleared what couldn't wait: the dead, the doors, the worst of the blood. Everyone else was left alone. Not everyone agrees on who the three should have been.</outcome>
        <ways><toil>1</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_WorkParty"><label>the clearing up after the fight</label><target>Colony</target><count>3</count><tasks><li>Corpses</li><li>Repair</li><li>Clean</li></tasks><duration>2~3</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Compromise</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmSoc_Reshuffled</thought><chance>0.3</chance></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_StrainRelief"><target>Others</target><amount>3</amount></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Who sits up with the sick ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_DlmC_NightNurse</defName>
    <label>who sits up with the sick</label>
    <weight>1</weight>
    <cooldownDays>30</cooldownDays>
    <minMedicine>1</minMedicine>
    <roleA>
      <sick>true</sick>
      <adult>false</adult>
    </roleA>
    <roleB>
      <bestAt>Medicine</bestAt>
      <minOpinionOfA>-20</minOpinionOfA>
    </roleB>
    <texts>
      <li>{A_nameDef} is no better tonight. {B_nameDef} could sit up with {A_objective}, and be no use to anyone tomorrow. There is medicine on the shelf, but not much of it.</li>
      <li>[winter] {A_nameDef} is shivering under two blankets, and {ILLNESS} isn't letting go. Somebody should be with {A_objective} tonight. {B_nameDef} has offered, and so has the medicine shelf.</li>
    </texts>
    <defaultOption>0</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>{B_nameDef} sits up with {A_objective} tonight</label>
        <outcome>{B_nameDef} sat up with {A_nameDef} through the night, kept the cloth cool and the water coming. {A_nameDef} is a little better. {B_nameDef} is yawning into breakfast.</outcome>
        <ways><mercy>3</mercy></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Visit"><label>{B_nameDef} sitting up with {A_nameDef}</label><who>B</who><whom>A</whom><hours>20~1</hours><duration>3~4</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_DlmL_Nursed</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_EaseIllness"><target>A</target><severity>0.1</severity></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>B</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Helped</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Hediff"><target>B</target><hediff>Council_Dlm_Sleepless</hediff></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>A dose from the stores, and everyone sleeps</label>
        <outcome>{B_nameDef} brought {A_nameDef} a dose from the shelf and went to bed. {A_nameDef} slept through, and the shelf has one less on it.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>1</generosity></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Consume"><what>medicine</what><count>1</count></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Visit"><label>{B_nameDef} bringing {A_nameDef} a dose</label><who>B</who><whom>A</whom><duration>0.5~0.75</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_EaseIllness"><target>A</target><severity>0.12</severity><immunity>0.05</immunity></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_DlmL_TimeToMend</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmL_StoresBare</thought><degreeTrait>Nerves</degreeTrait><maxDegree>-1</maxDegree></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Take turns through the night</label>
        <outcome>Three of them kept watch beside {A_nameDef} into the night, and {B_nameDef} got a whole night's sleep for once.</outcome>
        <ways><mercy>2</mercy><toil>1</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Vigil"><label>the watch beside {A_nameDef}</label><target>Others</target><count>3</count><to>Person</to><whom>A</whom><hours>20~2</hours><duration>2~3</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_DlmL_Nursed</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_EaseIllness"><target>A</target><severity>0.04</severity></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>B</target><thought>Council_DlmL_SharedTheLoad</thought></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Lessons or walls ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_DlmC_TeachOrBuild</defName>
    <label>lessons or walls</label>
    <weight>1</weight>
    <cooldownDays>40</cooldownDays>
    <busyTime>true</busyTime>
    <roleA>
      <passion>Construction</passion>
    </roleA>
    <roleB>
      <bestAt>Construction</bestAt>
      <minOpinionOfA>-10</minOpinionOfA>
    </roleB>
    <texts>
      <li>{A_nameDef} has been asking {B_nameDef} for lessons in building for weeks. Now the work is piling up, and {B_nameDef} says it's lessons or walls, not both.</li>
      <li>[afterraid] Half the walls need mending, and {A_nameDef} picks this week to ask {B_nameDef} to teach {A_objective} properly. {B_nameDef} doesn't say no. {B_nameDef} asks the council which it should be.</li>
    </texts>
    <defaultOption>2</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>Lessons now</label>
        <outcome>{B_nameDef} took {A_nameDef} through the work slowly, explaining every joint. Not much got built today. {A_nameDef} came away covered in sawdust and very pleased.</outcome>
        <ways><openness>2</openness><toil>-2</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Lesson"><label>{A_nameDef}'s building lesson</label><skill>Construction</skill><xpPerHour>200</xpPerHour><duration>2~3</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_DlmL_LearningATrade</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Trust"><target>A</target><amount>3</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmSoc_Reshuffled</thought><chance>0.4</chance></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Learn on the job, building beside {B_nameDef}</label>
        <outcome>{A_nameDef} carried and held while {B_nameDef} built, and picked up what {A_pronoun} could between the two. The work got done. The lessons, mostly, didn't.</outcome>
        <ways><toil>3</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_WorkParty"><label>{A_nameDef} building beside {B_nameDef}</label><target>AAndB</target><count>2</count><tasks><li>Build</li><li>Repair</li></tasks><duration>2.5~3.5</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Learn"><target>A</target><skill>Construction</skill><xp>250</xp></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Compromise</thought></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>After the rush</label>
        <outcome>The lessons wait until the work slows. {B_nameDef} went back to the walls, and {A_nameDef} went back to asking.</outcome>
        <ways><toil>2</toil></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_WorkParty"><label>{B_nameDef} back on the walls</label><target>B</target><count>1</count><tasks><li>Build</li><li>Repair</li></tasks><duration>2.5~3.5</duration></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Ignored</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>B</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairsFair</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairsFair</thought><degreeTrait>Industriousness</degreeTrait><minDegree>1</minDegree></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

  <!-- ===================== Seed for the neighbours ===================== -->
  <ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>
    <defName>Council_DlmC_NeighboursSeed</defName>
    <label>seed for the neighbours</label>
    <workerClass>ColonyCouncil.DilemmaWorker_Faction</workerClass>
    <weight>0.9</weight>
    <cooldownDays>60</cooldownDays>
    <seasons><li>Spring</li></seasons>
    <thingCount>40</thingCount>
    <texts>
      <li>Word came from {FACTION}: their stores spoiled over the winter, and they'll have nothing to sow. They ask whether the colony can spare {COUNT} raw food to see them through to the first harvest. {A_nameDef} brought the message, and wants an answer for them.</li>
      <li>[colony:Generous] {FACTION} sent to ask, a little shamefaced, for {COUNT} raw food. They know the colony has helped before. Their winter stores rotted, and the planting is close.</li>
    </texts>
    <defaultOption>2</defaultOption>
    <options>
      <li>
        <label>Send it, and ask nothing</label>
        <outcome>{A_nameDef} carried the sacks down to the gate for {FACTION}'s courier, who thanked the colony for it. They'll remember who fed them this spring.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>5</generosity></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_CarryOut"><label>food for {FACTION}</label><what>rawfood</what><to>Gate</to></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Goodwill"><amount>10</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_DlmR_KeptOurName</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_FairsFair</thought><onlyTrait><li>Kind</li></onlyTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_Dlm_Squandered</thought><onlyTrait><li>Greedy</li></onlyTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>Sell it to them at a fair price</label>
        <outcome>{FACTION}'s courier counted out the silver at the gate and took the sacks. A fair price, they said, and didn't smile saying it.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>-1</generosity></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_CarryOut"><label>food sold to {FACTION}</label><what>rawfood</what><to>Gate</to></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Spawn"><thing>Silver</thing><count>40</count><by>Outsiders</by></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Goodwill"><amount>4</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_DlmR_KeptOurName</thought></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmR_StoresSafe</thought><onlyTrait><li>Greedy</li></onlyTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
      <li>
        <label>The colony can't spare it</label>
        <outcome>The answer went back to {FACTION}: nothing to spare this year. The stores stay full, and {A_nameDef} didn't enjoy carrying that message.</outcome>
        <ways><generosity>-4</generosity></ways>
        <effects>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Goodwill"><amount>-4</amount></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>A</target><thought>Council_DlmL_TurnedAwayHungry</thought><exceptTrait><li>Greedy</li></exceptTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmR_StoresSafe</thought><onlyTrait><li>Greedy</li></onlyTrait></li>
          <li Class="ColonyCouncil.DilemmaEffect_Thought"><target>Others</target><thought>Council_DlmL_TurnedAwayHungry</thought><onlyTrait><li>Kind</li></onlyTrait></li>
        </effects>
      </li>
    </options>
  </ColonyCouncil.DilemmaDef>

</Defs>
